<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Exp Med</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Experimental Medicine</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0022-1007</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-9538</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">6182264</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2186837</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">15651557</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Articles</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Alpha and beta chains of SB and DR antigens are structurally distinct</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Hurley</surname><given-names>CK</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Shaw</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Nadler</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Schlossman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Capra</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>1</day><month>11</month><year>1982</year></pub-date><volume>156</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>1557</fpage><lpage>1562</lpage><permissions></permissions><abstract><p>Limited amino-terminal amino acid sequences of the HLA-controlled SB and DR antigens from the cell line PREISS (DR4/4, SB3/4) show differences in both the alpha and beta chain sequences of the two molecules. SB antigens, like DR antigens, appear to be homologues of the murine I-E antigens.</p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>